# Optional external assistant backend.
#
# When set, the app sends assistant requests to
#   <VITE_ASSISTANT_API_URL>/v1/assistant/requests
# instead of the relative path handled by the Vite dev proxy.
#
# Rules:
# - must be an absolute http(s) URL with no query or fragment;
# - use HTTPS for any hosted backend (http is acceptable only for
#   localhost development);
# - a malformed value renders a normalized "configuration" error —
#   the app never silently falls back and never fakes responses;
# - when unset or the backend is unreachable, the app renders its
#   normalized "unavailable" state.
#
# Configuration paths:
# - dev / WebContainer: put the variable in web/.env.local (read at
#   vite startup);
# - production build: the value is baked in at build time:
#     VITE_ASSISTANT_API_URL=https://backend.example npm run build
#
# The backend must also allow this app's exact origin via
# ONESHOT_CORS_ORIGINS (see openai_project/assistant_backend/README.md).
#
# VITE_ASSISTANT_API_URL=https://backend.example.com

# Optional visual capture backend proxy target.
# Used by the Vite dev server to proxy /v1/visual/* requests.
# Default: http://127.0.0.1:8000
# ONESHOT_VISUAL_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8000
